## 5. Adaptive Schwierigkeit & Lernratenanpassung

### 5.1 Dynamic Difficulty Adjustment (DDA)

```java
public class DifficultyAdapter {
    private double targetSuccessRate = 0.75;  // 75% Erfolgsquote ideal
    private double currentDifficulty = 1.0;
    
    public void adjust(boolean lastChallengeSucceeded) {
        if (lastChallengeSucceeded) {
            currentDifficulty *= 1.05;  // 5% schwieriger
        } else {
            currentDifficulty *= 0.95;  // 5% leichter
        }
        
        // Clamp zwischen 0.5 und 2.0
        currentDifficulty = Math.max(0.5, Math.min(2.0, currentDifficulty));
    }
    
    public double getDifficulty() {
        return currentDifficulty;
    }
}
```

**Prinzip:** Spieler soll immer im "Flow" sein – weder unter- noch überfordert.

### 5.2 Lernraten-Monitoring

```java
public class LearningRateTracker {
    private List<Double> recentScores = new ArrayList<>();
    private int windowSize = 10;
    
    public void recordScore(double score) {
        recentScores.add(score);
        if (recentScores.size() > windowSize) {
            recentScores.remove(0);
        }
    }
    
    public double getAverageImprovement() {
        if (recentScores.size() < 2) return 0.0;
        
        double firstHalf = recentScores.subList(0, recentScores.size() / 2)
            .stream().mapToDouble(Double::doubleValue).average().orElse(0.0);
        double secondHalf = recentScores.subList(recentScores.size() / 2, recentScores.size())
            .stream().mapToDouble(Double::doubleValue).average().orElse(0.0);
        
        return secondHalf - firstHalf;
    }
    
    public boolean isLearning() {
        return getAverageImprovement() > 0.05;  // >5% Verbesserung
    }
}
```

